cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "ThinkDrag: Semantic Drag-Based Image Editing with Visual Reasoning"
abstract: "ThinkDrag is a unified multimodal framework for drag-based image editing with visual reasoning. It interprets sparse drag handles as semantic object- and scene-level transformations, can optionally produce an explicit reasoning trace before image generation, and grounds each drag with Drag Endpoint Markers. The work also introduces a supervised dataset of semantic drag transformations with reasoning traces and DragBench++, a benchmark of challenging drag-based editing scenarios with reference edits."
